sthrone[0] | 66, 6, 24, 24 | The throne, drawn on the room's centre tile, for row 0 of 5 of the player's levels (MIR, EMIR and AMARIR in vanilla). As painted it's for a throne room placed 5 tiles wide without turning; the game turns it for the other three ways.
sthrone[4] | 66, 42, 24, 24 | The throne, drawn on the room's centre tile, for row 1 of 5 of the player's levels (PRONTIX, APPRONTIX and APPRONTIX_RAY in vanilla). As painted it's for a throne room placed 5 tiles wide without turning; the game turns it for the other three ways.
sthrone[8] | 66, 78, 24, 24 | The throne, drawn on the room's centre tile, for row 2 of 5 of the player's levels (LEGATI, LEGATI_RAY and DAKORI in vanilla). As painted it's for a throne room placed 5 tiles wide without turning; the game turns it for the other three ways.
sthrone[12] | 66, 114, 24, 24 | The throne, drawn on the room's centre tile, for row 3 of 5 of the player's levels (DAKORI_RAY, SORAX and SORAX_RAY in vanilla). As painted it's for a throne room placed 5 tiles wide without turning; the game turns it for the other three ways.
sthrone[16] | 66, 150, 24, 24 | The throne, drawn on the room's centre tile, for row 4 of 5 of the player's levels (ASTA and ASTA_RAY in vanilla). As painted it's for a throne room placed 5 tiles wide without turning; the game turns it for the other three ways.
